Part 1 · linearity of expectation for two fair dice
E[X + Y] by enumeration over 36 outcomes = 7
E[X] + E[Y] = 7
the two agree: True
Part 2 · one roll, a paid reroll of 100 cents, payoff 100 cents per face
continuation value after paying the fee: 250 cents
face 1: stop pays 100 cents, best action reroll
face 2: stop pays 200 cents, best action reroll
face 3: stop pays 300 cents, best action stop
face 4: stop pays 400 cents, best action stop
face 5: stop pays 500 cents, best action stop
face 6: stop pays 600 cents, best action stop
value of the game by backward induction = 1150/3 cents (383.33 to two places)
best of all 64 stopping policies by enumeration = 1150/3 cents
backward induction equals the best policy: True
stop on every face (no reroll) = 350 cents
Part 3 · stopping rules over 6 turns, fair game (+100 or -100, probability 1/2 each)
play all turns: expectation 0 (sequences: 0)
stop after the first win: expectation 0 (sequences: 0)
stop after the first loss: expectation 0 (sequences: 0)
stop when the total reaches 100 cents: expectation 0 (sequences: 0)
stop at 200 cents of gain or loss: expectation 0 (sequences: 0)
the two methods agree for every rule: True
the expectation is 0 for every rule: True
Part 3b · the same rules on a biased game (+150 or -100, probability 1/2 each)
play all turns: expectation 150
stop after the first win: expectation 1575/32
stop after the first loss: expectation 1575/32
stop when the total reaches 100 cents: expectation 575/8
stop at 200 cents of gain or loss: expectation 625/8
